Customer Problem Statements & System Requirements 
Problem Statement: 
A visit to the doctor’s office or hospital is often met with stress from the start. It does not help that upon arrival, the patient is expected to fill out paperwork that feels excessive. There are many forms that patients fill out each time they enter a healthcare setting. There are still hospitals that use paper records instead of electronic file keeping, which can slow down the process of receiving results and make it more difficult for patients to access their health information.  
A new patient tracker system should be electronic and keep all patient information and records in one easily accessible place. Patients should be able to log into the system to set up appointments, see test results, and access other relevant health information. This would speed up getting answers about health concerns and allow patients to stay involved in their own health. Patients would not have to wait for calls from providers and administration, the information would all be available to them immediately. 
Glossary of Terms: 
•	Appointment Management- Schedule, reschedule, or cancel appointments 
•	Reminders- Notifications sent straight to a patient’s phone or email address, reminding them to confirm appointments.   
•	Medical Record- A patient’s medical history with past and current health issues. Test results and patient medications should also be listed here.  
•	Patient tracker- A portal for patients to see all their health information in one place. 
