Functional Requirements Specification of Patient Tracker System
Stakeholders
•	Patients
•	Providers and Staff
•	Admiration Workers
Actors and Goals
•	Primary Actors
o	Patients can access all their medical records via the patient tracker system. They can set up an account without assistance or work. They can schedule appointments and request prescription refills from their doctors. Patients should be able to view their test results and even chat with their provider directly within the system. 
o	Doctors and Staff can view their schedules and make changes as needed. They can see all their patients in the system. They can add to patients’ treatment plans, fill prescriptions, and answer questions the patient asks. 
•	Secondary Actors
o	Administration Workers can go into the patient tracker system and manage appointments and add to the doctors’ schedules. They can basically do everything for the patient via the system, but getting patients involved in their healthcare by giving them full access is the point of the patient tracker system. 
Use Cases
•	Patient can create an account on their own (2).
•	Patients can view full medical records (3).
•	Patients can view their current treatment plans (2).
•	Patients can schedule, reschedule, and cancel appointments in the system (3). 
•	Patients can request prescription refills (3).
•	Patients can view their test results (3).
•	Patients can talk with their providers (4).
•	Providers can view their schedules (2).
•	Providers can view patients (2).
•	Providers can add to the patient treatment plans (3).
•	Providers can fill prescriptions (3).
•	Providers can communicate with their patients (4).
•	Administrators can manage appointments (3).
•	Administrators can schedule new appointments and add them to the provider schedules (3).
